Demonstration of Proposed Features
1. Introduction

The project demonstration explains the major features implemented in the ServiceNow Script-Controlled ACL solution.

2. User Creation

The demonstration begins by showing the creation of the required users in ServiceNow.

The users are used to test different access permissions.

3. Role Creation

The required roles are created and assigned to the appropriate users.

These roles are used as part of the ACL access-control mechanism.

4. Table Creation

A custom table named:

u_institution_details

is created to store student and institution-related information.

5. Record Creation

Sample records are created with different values in the Branch field.

The available branch choices are:

ECE
EEE
CSE
6. READ Access

The READ ACL is demonstrated by testing whether users can view records according to the configured access conditions.

7. CREATE Access

The CREATE ACL is demonstrated by testing whether authorized users can create new records.

8. WRITE Access

The WRITE ACL is demonstrated by attempting to modify existing records using users with different permissions.

9. DELETE Access

The DELETE ACL is demonstrated by testing whether users with the required permissions can delete records.

10. Administrator Access

Administrator access is demonstrated to verify that administrators can perform the required management activities.

11. Final Output

The final demonstration shows that the configured ACLs control access to the institution records according to the defined roles and conditions.

12. Conclusion

The demonstration provides a practical view of the project's implementation and shows how ServiceNow ACLs can be used to control record-level access.
